# Independent review: supplementary fixed-budget MCQ nonregression

Review prepared on 2026-10-25 UTC, before any candidate quality output according to the coordinator.
This is a proposed, separately named supplementary protocol, informed by observed native
calibration. It is not the original preregistered endpoint and does not replace either strict
completion gate. Adoption and any new offline scorer must be frozen and hashed before the first raw
or grouped candidate quality output. Existing producer, scorer, plans and attempts remain unchanged.

## Decision and preserved failures

The existing strict v1 and v2 condition requires every selected request to finish without output-cap
truncation. Both conditions have already failed in native controls. In particular, v2 cannot regain
a strict pass by collecting the remaining questions. Continue the frozen 8192-token v2 collection to
measure the separate fixed-budget outcome; do not raise the cap again, remove cases, retry selected
answers, change prompts/parser, or label a supplementary pass `full_frozen_plan_passed`.

A scientifically useful supplementary estimand is: **the proportion of the same 200 questions for
which this exact runtime returns a valid gold-matching final answer before its fixed 8192-token
limit**. A length-limited response is an observed unsuccessful answer under this definition. That
allows complete fixed-budget response collection despite some unsuccessful answers. The original
scorer already applies precisely this conservative per-question correctness rule; no answer
previously marked wrong becomes correct under this proposal.

Recommended name: `supplementary_budgeted_mcq_nonregression_v1`. Report its answer nonregression
result and mixed-work coverage separately, and retain the strict gate results alongside them. A
supplementary pass cannot by itself mark Issue #23 resolved, numerically qualify PR10, or establish
general model quality.

